# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, a clone made on a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows /
# WSL default) gets a CRLF working tree, while the Composer dist tarball is LF — so the
# clone differs from the installed package on *every* line, and `diff` against `vendor/`
# is useless. `text=auto` stores everything as LF in the repository regardless of the
# contributor's platform, and `eol=lf` checks it back out as LF for everyone.
#
# Safe to add to an existing repo here: these modules are published from a Linux staging
# dir, so their blobs are already LF and adding this triggers no renormalisation.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary formats — normalising them corrupts the file.
# (SVG is deliberately absent: the bundled flag assets are text and should be normalised.)
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary
*.phar binary
